.TH CONDUCTOR-FILES 8 "2026-10-03" "Samba Conductor" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
conductor-files \- Samba Conductor agent for domain-member file servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conductor-files
.I command
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conductor-files
lets Samba Conductor manage the shares of a Samba domain-member file
server: shares in the registry configuration (net conf), access by AD group
SID applied as NT ACLs, and live sessions. It refuses to run on a domain
controller. conductor connects over TLS 1.3 with both keys pinned; a
conductor instance is trusted only after a one-time enrollment code made on
the file server. The default configuration is
.IR /etc/conductor-files/agent.toml .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the agent (started by
.BR conductor-files.service ).
.TP
.B enroll-code [\-\-ttl 1h] [\-\-quiet]
Print a one-time enrollment code (as root).
.TP
.B enroll-cancel
Cancel the outstanding code.
.TP
.B trust list | trust remove PIN
Pinned conductor keys.
.TP
.B check
Check the prerequisites (every line must be ok).
.TP
.B audit verify
Check the hash-chained audit log.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-files/agent.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/conductor-files.service.d/roots.conf
Drop-in that makes the share roots writable for the unit.
.TP
.I /var/lib/conductor-files/
Key pair, pinned keys, outstanding code, audit log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conductor (8),
.BR net (8),
.BR smb.conf (5)
